{"attack":true,"case":"The target's distinguishing evidence does not distinguish genuine reliability from mere compliance.\nThe problem requires evidence within a single evaluation that separates a genuine reliability gain from mere checklist compliance that merely tracks the right answer. The target offers 'Corrective Friction'—initial disagreement followed by reasoned convergence—as that evidence. But friction (divergence-convergence) does not entail reliability: mere compliance can produce friction, and genuine reliability can be frictionless. The target never operationalizes how the convergence (vs mere compliance) tracks the verifiable outcome independently of the outcome itself.\ncites: 323b58d0b22c5942f01dcfbc3d30fbaf6b1d12a82c6e35d8c3fe1498e357c214","counterexample":[{"scenario":"Panel B (same friction, wrong outcome): the panel rejects the same checklist item and debates, then converges to the wrong answer."},{"scenario":"Panel C (mere compliance): the panel linearly checks items without friction and still arrives at the right answer."}]}